--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Test Description
-- This tests the receive functionality for accepting maximum sized 
-- frames in 10 or 100 mode operation.
--
-- This version of the test is run with the RX descriptor buffer size set to 
-- 1536 bytes, such that one max length packet is contained in one buffer.
-- 
-- Functional Coverage  																																																																											  tion.
-- · Ensures that the GEM will only accept a frame up to the maximum size 
--   of 1518 bytes in 100 mode operation.
-- · Ensure that the GEM can also accept maximum sized frames of 1536 bytes 
--   when configured properly in 100 mode operation.
-- 
-- Detailed Test Description
-- Receiving Long Frames (1518 bytes):
-- 1. Initialise the GEM for 100 mode operation.
-- 2. Receive a frame that is 1519 bytes long.
-- 3. Receive a frame that is 1518 bytes long.
-- 4. Check the status and statistics registers and ensure that the above operations 
--    were handled properly. Should be one excessive length frame and the appropriate 
--    bucket counter should be incremented.
-- Receiving Long Frames (1536 bytes):
-- 5. Enable the GEM to receive frames which are 1536 bytes long.
-- 6. Receive a frame that is 1537 bytes long.
-- 7. Receive a frame that is 1536 bytes long.
-- 8. Check the status and statistics registers and ensure that the above operations 
--    were handled properly. Should be one excessive length frame and the appropriate 
--    bucket counter should be incremented.
-- 9. Receive a frame that is 1000 bytes long
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

apbrd(100) 00 00000000  -- check reset value of network control register
apbrd      04 00080000  -- check reset value of network config register
apbwr      04 00280001  -- indicate 100M operation, will check pin l8r.
apbrd      04 00280001  -- verify write to speed register..
apbrd      18 00000000  -- check reset value of receive queue pointer
apbwr      18 66660000  -- write receive queue pointer
apbrd      18 66660000  -- check receive queue pointer
apbwr      00 00000004  -- enable receive and trigger reception of frame
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbwr      28 ffffffff  -- enable all interrupts
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbwr      98 12345678  -- specific address register 3 bottom
apbwr      9C 00001111  -- specific address register 3 top
apbrd      08 00000006  -- check reset value of network status register
apbwr      10 001801d0  -- set AHB burst size to 16 & RX system buffer to 1536
apbrdf     20 00000000  -- check contents of the receive status register 

